{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1087957-mystery-meta-spheres","id":1087957,"title":"Mystery/Meta Spheres.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-04T15:46:43-07:00","id":1087957,"title":"Mystery/Meta Spheres.","content":"So, I've been considering the idea of 'secret' spheres. As it is, most mages abilities are fairly cut and dry. You generally can at least GUESS at 'how' that was done. Someone hurls a fireball? Forces was probably involved. A car was transformed into a pig? Life and Matter.<br /> <br /> But then you have the oddball cases where the spheres don't seem to easily apply.<br /> <br /> And it occurs to me. That there could be <i>secret</i> spheres. You make them up as ST at the start of the game. Throw in NPC's who make use of them. For example, a Meta Sphere that manipulates magic itself. In general, they should be formulated in such a way as to <i>not make sense</i> to the PCs ideas of how magic works. For example, being able to do something that in one of the standard spheres requires a very high level of mastery. But in this new mystery sphere is fairly low key. For example, a mystery sphere of Transferrance. It deals with taking something from one thing and giving it to another. You can create a material that's radioactive with fairly basic Transferrance + Matter. But normally that takes high levels of Forces and Matter. This is probably a terrible idea but it was something I thought of given a few minutes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11744,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","user":"Enginseer-42","date":". 05-04-2017, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T16:10:55-07:00","id":1087971,"title":"","content":"I had similar thoughts. I was thinking of Death and Fate spheres before Mage the Awakening, and things like a sphere system with a sphere for air, earth, fire, water, and aether, used by some obscure group of mages. I was also trying to make something for the 5 elements in Chinese philosphy and the 7 chakras but didn't get very far with those. I never did do anything with the ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T03:12:06-07:00","id":1088169,"title":"","content":"So, my first thought was &quot;This is a terrible idea.&quot; but then I got thinking. Why should'nt there be mages with different paradigms that are based on an entirely different sphere system? This would be an excelent way of making your PCs and players wonder what is actually happening. Though it might be hard to make an alternative system work. Then again, maybe that paradigm is flawed in it's own ways and while it is more potent in some ways, as the Transferrance spere, it is utterly impossible to do other things, regular sphere magic can easily acomplish.<br /> <br /> Thinking further about this, I am now back at a point, where I think: &quot;Wouldn't all this be possible with regular sphere magic as well? This is exactly what paradigm is all about.&quot;<br /> Difficult topic...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T03:27:00-07:00","id":1088174,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing it would be best to think of these as models of reality with their own quirks and flaws and the 9 spheres system simply as the latest model in the WoD.<br /> Heck, I'd take the whole Entropy sphere as kind of a flaw in the 9 sphere system and as a sign that people in the WoD consider that the world is fated to die.<br /> <br /> I told a player once that I'd allow them to play a custom sphere if they could design it from Level 1 to 5. It never happened though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T03:47:02-07:00","id":1088182,"title":"","content":"Well, there is the Minor Sphere option. If you wanted, you could give NPCs their own Minor Spheres, tailored to certain themes. Hell, I might be inclined to do that as a matter of course, simply for the sake of boiling down an NPC's capabilities to essentials for their practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T04:33:22-07:00","id":1088196,"title":"","content":"The Revised Storytellers guide had those custom spheres, I think that is what Blueecho is talking about. So you could have say a Fire Sphere, and it not only allows the control of flames, but their spirits of fire, and the very concept of burning.<br /> <br /> Its a fun option, and can be cool for the NPCs, or even players if you help them handle it. It reminds a bit of tapping into Dark Age Mage Magic. So why not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T04:49:49-07:00","id":1088205,"title":"","content":"As for a kind of &quot;Meta&quot; Sphere - a Sphere of Magick itself - that would either be Prime, or the mythical Tenth Sphere. Which, obviously, shouldn't just be out there in the wild, when mages have been looking for it for centuries.<br /> <br /> That said, fragments of the Tenth Sphere might manifest themselves in the personal magickal styles of a rare few assorted Orphans. Might provide clues that a mage scholar could follow to develop the true Tenth Sphere. That would be a story hook, if you're into that sort of thing. (Personally, I always found the Tenth Sphere to be one of the less interesting parts of Mage lore).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T09:15:05-07:00","id":1088324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, they should be formulated in such a way as to <i>not make sense</i> to the PCs ideas of how magic works. For example, being able to do something that in one of the standard spheres requires a very high level of mastery. But in this new mystery sphere is fairly low key. For example, a mystery sphere of Transferrance. It deals with taking something from one thing and giving it to another. You can create a material that's radioactive with fairly basic Transferrance + Matter. But normally that takes high levels of Forces and Matter. This is probably a terrible idea but it was something I thought of given a few minutes.</div> </div> </div> </div>You be just defined Minor Spheres (exept for them being &quot;minor&quot;, or less abarcative than regular ones, which I think it's unnecessary). Also DA: Mage Pillars (exept that there everyone uses them)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For example, a Meta Sphere that manipulates magic itself. </div> </div> </div>The Sphere that manipulates magick its Prime. What's &quot;magick&quot; but an alteration of the tapestry of reality...and that tapestry it's made of Prime (the Avatar itself it's a &quot;Shard of Prime&quot;). That's why you use it to do &quot;offensive countermagick&quot;, and unweaving, and to create Artifacts imbued with magick...<br /> <br /> Meta-magick, like in D&amp;D to empower a spell or make it last longer, it's not permited for game balance reasons. You can do it in a very restricted manner, if you use the same Sphere to cast the same Effect, but with more successes. You can do better metamagick with Archspheres (like Forces 6 that gives x2 successes, Or multiple level 7 that allows to affect multiple objetives with 1 success, or Spirit 9 that, by awakening someone, implies to be able to grant Arete). A Metasphere that allows that would be more than a little OP, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-05-2017, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T04:17:51-07:00","id":1088695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1087957-mystery-meta-spheres?p=1088324#post1088324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meta-magick, like in D&amp;D to empower a spell or make it last longer, it's not permited for game balance reasons. You can do it in a very restricted manner, if you use the same Sphere to cast the same Effect, but with more successes. You can do better metamagick with Archspheres (like Forces 6 that gives x2 successes, Or multiple level 7 that allows to affect multiple objetives with 1 success, or Spirit 9 that, by awakening someone, implies to be able to grant Arete). A Metasphere that allows that would be more than a little OP, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spells in DnD are prepared, something a mage in Mage can and should also do. So preparing a spell with meta-magic effects (stronger, last longer etc) is just preparing a spell with more successes. It's just that easy. Difference in the systems: Mages in Mage can spontaniously cast simpler spells and preparing a more complex spell means you can just prepare less spells in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T15:19:01-07:00","id":1088876,"title":"","content":"I prefer the term <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/784502-composite-spheres-for-orphans\">Composite Spheres</a>. That said, I prefer my Traditions to have <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/88705-sphere-variants-for-the-traditions\"> Sphere variants </a> to represent the special insights that one Tradition might have concerning a particular Sphere above and beyond what the Traditions as a whole know about it; and I like my non-Traditions having <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/441968-pillars-for-the-modern-crafts\"> whole systems of magic </a> with their own organizing principles that don't neatly line up with the Spheres. For instance, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/758179-fields-for-the-technocracy\">the Technocracy </a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T19:24:14-07:00","id":1088956,"title":"","content":"Has anyone ran a chronicle with the minor spheres? I created several of them and used them alongside the major spheres in a chronicle that ran for over 40 sessions (I made minor spheres 25% cheaper than the nine major spheres).<br /> <br /> I found that the minor spheres were interesting but the interplay betweven the major spheres was greater in most cases. The minor spheres were often used without other spheres (with the exception of correspondence or the sphere of Travel which allowed for magic to be done at range), I found them less likely to be used in multi sphere rotes which made the game feel less satisfying.<br /> <br /> Does anybody have any thoughts on this. I like the minor spheres but my major experience in using them was somewhat disappointing them.<br /> <br /> Lastly, I created numerous minor spheres, here's a list of a few for relevance<br /> <br /> Travel: Allows one to travel distances, move unimpeeded and and perform magic from a distance. No manipulation of space directly but does allow for teleportation in the physical world and the umbra. Inspired by the Valderman pillar Fara.<br /> <br /> Beast: Life, Mind and some Spirit effects as they relate to animals.<br /> <br /> Storms/Weather: Forces, Prime and Spirit as it pertains to weather and to some degree motion. This one was basically the sphere of fire with a different element.<br /> <br /> Body: Life and Prime effects with an akashic focus on chi and life force, very limited shape shifting, largely based around humanoids.<br /> <br /> Fortune: Curses and Blessings, inspired by the Valderman pillar Forlog which also allows one to be well received by others.<br /> <br /> Harmony: This focused on healing with life and mind as well as some prime effects that could remove resonance that was deemed harmful (Dreamspeaker and Verbena based)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T22:06:11-07:00","id":1089001,"title":"","content":"Quite simply, it's not easy to make a Sphere. And there's no guidelines. Sphere system it's made so each Sphere has something to give to the others, they're all inter-related trough the methaphysics of magick. Have you designed the mini spheres with this kind of connections in mind?.<br /> <br /> Heres how I think the concepts you described could be used in conjunctions:<br /> <br /> Body sounds limmited, but I can see as working for a ton of enhancements and crazy matial arts movements. For instance, I may let someone with Body enchant human life pattern at Body 3-4, like as if he was using prime 4-5 (Training from hell that get's supernatural results <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), obviously, this may need other spheres to get realy weird gains. Shapeshifting may be limmited, but at least at level 5 I would allow it to transcend the human form (to have a body of light, become like the river, join with nature, be the mountain, and stuff like that)-of course, in conjunction with the propper Spheres. As more concrete examples: I can see a Body 1-2 / Time 1 rote to adapt the rithm of your body to that of the opponent (timing the opponent's moves and adjusting your own body so you can counter them), a Body 3 / Forces 2 that allows to add the force of your opponent to your next blow (possibly trading damage received for extra Strength in your next blow to a greater degree that what you could get with Body alone)...etc.<br /> I like it.<br /> <br /> Travel it's self explanatory, but don't let it be just &quot;the teleport sphere&quot;, travel includes knowledge of the path, alteration and creation of pathways, an understanding of movement, including the potential to block or alter the travel for someone. No manipulation of space?, then what happens when I want to destroy the possibility to travel somewhere (essentially ending the posibility to reach a place)?<br /> <br /> Storms/Weather: This one I find interesting because it's hard to make rain with the Spheres, I guess this makes it easy. In conjunction it's could be more impressive and vulgar...like, say, combine it with Fire, and get a rain of fire (at a ludicrously low level for such a massive shenanigan, I imagine), with Life and get a rain of frogs or to alter the relationships between weather and life (like,say, to create plants that can grow in the worst dry wheaters). It's Forces, just that it's very, very, very limmited (in the true spirit of mini spheres) and even less subtle when used in conjunction (or at least I can't think of a good, subtle, conjunctional effect right now).<br /> <br /> Fortune...you can get most of this Sphere with, like, Entropy 3. But I can see Fate being it's own thing. Basically, it takes the most useful aspect of Entropy and uses it alone. Use it in conjunction just like you would with Entropy...No big difficulty there. (Personally, I would include fortunetelling as part of Fortune, and allow Fortune to trigger spells like Time 4 for those nasty conditional curses)<br /> <br /> Harmony. Well, I don't understand the concept.<br /> On one hand if it is the just the restoration Sphere you seem to describe, it will deprive one of the power to twist the concept in fun ways. The general concept of a Healing Sphere will never work well with other Spheres. because it's too specific (What's Forces + Healing?, to heal a fire?)<br /> On the other hand, If I ignore the moral behind the sphere and start toying with the concept I can't see what you &quot;can't&quot; do with it (Want to cause a conflict, disharmonize people. Want to get a girl, make your relation harmonious. Want to heal, harmonize the life pattern, want to attack, disharmonize the life pattern)...which it's equaly bad, if you want it to be used with others.<br /> Harmony seems either to vage or too limited as a concept to me. You need to create dependences, draw a line, state where it can be use and where it can't work alone and needs conjunction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-07-2017, 01:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T03:20:44-07:00","id":1089053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1087957-mystery-meta-spheres?p=1088956#post1088956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone ran a chronicle with the minor spheres? I created several of them and used them alongside the major spheres in a chronicle that ran for over 40 sessions (I made minor spheres 25% cheaper than the nine major spheres).<br /> <br /> I found that the minor spheres were interesting but the interplay betweven the major spheres was greater in most cases. The minor spheres were often used without other spheres (with the exception of correspondence or the sphere of Travel which allowed for magic to be done at range), I found them less likely to be used in multi sphere rotes which made the game feel less satisfying.<br /> <br /> Does anybody have any thoughts on this. I like the minor spheres but my major experience in using them was somewhat disappointing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd use minor spheres only in a game, where the mages would have a rather limited paradigm. You could replace the old sphere system to allow players to actually build their own spheres. This could either be in an orphan game, where other mages, like the Traditions, still use normal spheres and are very powerfull in comparison. Or everyone would use just a few minor spheres, gaining quick mastery over their chosen aspect, but never mastering the whole of magic. The latter would very much limit the power of mages to a degree, where they wouldn't overpower other supernaturals easily, making the power scaling more predictible.<br /> <br /> Using these spheres alongside the greater spheres doesn't make much sense, since they easily get replaced later on, in long games at least. And about using minor spheres in conjunctional effects... they're already conjunctional effects of greater spheres, so there's no need for that, when you don't want to modify spell range, duration or want to include triggers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}